# No em-dashes

Do not use em-dashes (`—`) anywhere in user-facing portfolio copy (HTML text, titles, meta, alt text, labels, footers).

## Prefer instead

- **Titles / name separators:** middot (`·`), e.g. `Aashi Bhaiji · Information Designer`
- **Lists or asides in prose:** comma or colon
- **Two contrasting clauses:** period or colon (e.g. `not X. It was Y.`)
- **Footer:** `say hello` (no dash before the email)

## Allowed

- En-dashes (`–`) in numeric ranges only (e.g. `10–15`, `06–10`)
- Hyphens in compound words (e.g. `decision-ready`, `mobile-first`)

Apply this on every new or edited page going forward.
